    faqs: [{"q": "Is Kedarnath with Chopta Tungnath suitable for beginners?", "a": "Yes, but basic fitness is required due to long trekking distances."}, {"q": "Why should I combine Kedarnath and Chopta Tungnath in one trip?", "a": "Both destinations are located in the Garhwal Himalayas and can be conveniently covered in a single itinerary. Travelers get to experience sacred temples, Himalayan trekking, stunning mountain views, and beautiful alpine landscapes in one journey."}, {"q": "How many days are required for a Kedarnath and Chopta Tungnath trip?", "a": "A well-planned itinerary usually takes 5 to 7 days, depending on your starting location and sightseeing preferences."}, {"q": "What is the maximum altitude of the trip?", "a": "The highest point is Chandrashila Summit at approximately 13,123 ft."}, {"q": "How far is Chandrashila from Tungnath?", "a": "The Chandrashila summit is about 1.5 km beyond Tungnath Temple."}, {"q": "How difficult is the Kedarnath Trek?", "a": "It is considered moderate to challenging due to steep ascent and altitude."}, {"q": "Is Tungnath Trek difficult?", "a": "No, Tungnath Trek is easy to moderate and beginner-friendly."}, {"q": "What is the best time for Kedarnath with Chopta Tungnath Trek?", "a": "April to June and September to November are ideal seasons."}, {"q": "How difficult is the Chopta Tungnath Trek?", "a": "The trek is considered easy to moderate and is suitable for most travelers."}, {"q": "Are ponies and palkis available for Kedarnath?", "a": "Yes, pony and doli services are available at additional cost."}, {"q": "What type of accommodation is provided?", "a": "Hotels, camps, and tents depending on the destination."}, {"q": "Is mobile network available throughout the route?", "a": "Network connectivity is limited in high-altitude areas."}, {"q": "What should I carry for the trip?", "a": "Warm clothes, trekking shoes, rain gear, medicines, power bank, and ID proof."}, {"q": "Why is this journey spiritually important?", "a": "It combines Kedarnath Jyotirlinga, Tungnath Temple, Chandrashila Summit, and sacred Himalayan landscapes into one divine pilgrimage experience."}],
